{
  "_comment": [
    "Human ids are pinned deliberately. Identities live in an in-memory store and",
    "are reseeded on every boot, so an unpinned id would be regenerated each time.",
    "The id becomes the TAT 'sub', and a relying party keys the end user on that",
    "value: letting it drift would make every restart look like a brand-new user.",
    "Attributes are surfaced as custom claims in the TAT claim bags."
  ],
